# ARCHITECTURE RULES

## Feature-Based Organization

Group code by **feature domain**, not technical role. The project's feature folders are:

```
src/features/
  landing/           — landing page, example prompts
  simulation/        — debate stream, message parsing, prompt composer
  agents/            — personas, agent types, team templates
  artifacts/         — artifact panel, result display
  workspace/         — sidebar, runs dashboard, export, auth modals
```

Each feature folder contains its own components, hooks, actions, and types:

```
src/features/simulation/
  components/
  hooks/
  actions/
  types.ts
```

- Feature folders must not import from other feature folders directly. Use `src/lib/` or `src/shared/` as the integration layer.
- Shared code spanning multiple features lives in `src/lib/` (auth, db, export, rate-limit, workspace-url, etc.).

## Shared Kernel (`src/lib/`)

The shared kernel is stable — breaking changes cascade to every feature:

```
src/lib/
  auth/        — JWT, bcryptjs, guest sessions, auth schemas
  db/          — Prisma helpers, runs, projects, run-reconcile
  export/      — markdown, PDF generation, download blob
  ai/          — pricing, usage accumulation, persist-usage
  rate-limit.ts / rate-limit-config.ts / rate-limit-redis.ts / rate-limit-response.ts
  types.ts     — shared domain types
```

- Never put feature-specific logic in the shared kernel.
- A module file must not exceed **400 lines**. Split oversized files by responsibility.

## Import Ordering

Order imports in this sequence, separated by blank lines:

```typescript
// 1. Runtime guards
import "server-only";

// 2. External libraries
import { NextResponse } from "next/server";
import { prisma } from "@/lib/prisma";

// 3. Internal shared modules
import { requireRunAccess } from "@/lib/db/runs";
import type { RunOwnershipScope } from "@/lib/db/runs";

// 4. Relative imports (same feature)
import { parseMessageBlocks } from "./parse-message-blocks";
```

- Always use `import type` for type-only imports.
- Never mix type and value imports from the same module — use two `import` statements.

## Barrel File Discipline

Barrel files (`index.ts`) exist only for named re-exports:

```typescript
// src/features/simulation/index.ts
export { SimulationPanel } from "./components/simulation-panel";
export { useSimulationStream } from "./hooks/use-simulation-stream";
export type { SimulationState } from "./types";
```

- A barrel file must contain only `export` / `export type` statements. No functions, constants, or logic.
- Never `export *` — explicitly name every export so dead-code elimination and import tracing work.
- Circular imports are **forbidden**. Extract shared dependencies into a third module when two modules depend on each other.

## AI Flow Architecture

UI → Application → Orchestration → Provider. Never call LLM providers directly from UI components. See `04-ai-orchestration.mdc` for the full AI pipeline.
